{
  "approvedCollectionDeletionUpdate": "2026-10-19: CollectionViewSheets, CollectionRepository, TipTapContentAnalyzer, DocumentRepositories and CollectionTests updated for the requested cross-platform Delete Collection action. Existing tests are retained. Editor hosting and session baselines are unchanged.",
  "approvedMobileEditorUpdate": "2026-10-20: Only DocumentEditorView, TipTapWebView, TipTapEditorSession, CollectionKanbanView and CollectionDocumentIntegration baselines changed for the requested iPhone/iPad single-line page titles, divider insertion, slash dismissal and quote Backspace fixes. Mac implementations, shared editor resources, persistence, WebView ownership and teardown remain unchanged.",
  "approvedPhoneGalleryLoadingUpdate": "2026-10-20: DocumentBrowserView, TagBrowserView and LibraryDocumentPreview apply a 0.6 height fraction only on iPhone; existing iPad and Mac preview sizing and rendering are retained. VellixApp replaces library startup ProgressView with purple circular-dot loading on both iPhone and iPad. No persistence or startup behavior changes.",
  "approvedMobileBlockSelectionUpdate": "2026-10-20: TipTapWebView injects the iOS-only ProseMirror block-swipe extension before editor initialization; DocumentEditorView waits for authoritative mode acknowledgements. The existing editor artifact gains optional integration hooks mirrored in maintained backend source, without a build or bundler. Absent-provider Mac behavior, WebView ownership, loading, persistence and teardown are retained.",
  "approvedMobileBlockSelectionCorrections": "2026-10-20: Only the editor artifact baseline advances for optional iOS nested-deletion and transformation/snapshot hooks, mechanically mirrored from maintained source. The revised mobile plugin owns contact/input mapping, hierarchical selection, persistent ranges and aligned/table-visible painting. Native WebView ownership/lifecycle, Mac fallback, schemas, persistence and synchronization are unchanged; no build or bundler was run.",
  "approvedNativeNestedPageSpacing": "2026-10-20: Only DocumentEditorView advances for 12 points of top padding inside the nonempty native unplacedPages list, shared by plain and themed mobile layouts and by nested rows/cards. WebView ownership/lifecycle and Mac implementations are unchanged. The separately changed editor-bundle hash is not rebased by this spacing fix.",
  "approvedPhoneAllDocsPreviewHeight": "2026-10-20: Only DocumentBrowserView advances to restore ten percent of original preview height in the default iPhone All Docs gallery (0.6 to 0.7). Named Collections galleries, other browser modes, Tags, iPad and Mac sizing are unchanged. Preview rendering, top anchoring and widths are unchanged; no build was run.",
